---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<Layout title="Vaster Agent — The Staff Loan File | Zulo" description="How a private lender’s team went from hand-built committee packets to one loan file. People still make the credit decision." nav="work">
	<main id="main-content" class="transformation-page">
		<section class="page-masthead site-container case-intro">
			<a class="case-back" href="/work">← Selected work</a>
			<div class="case-title-row"><h1>Vaster Agent<span class="case-dot">.</span></h1></div>
			<p class="case-deck">How a private lender’s team went from hand-built committee packets to one loan file.</p>
			<dl class="project-facts">
				<div><dt>CLIENT</dt><dd>Vaster</dd></div>
				<div><dt>SECTOR</dt><dd>Private lending</dd></div>
				<div><dt>THE WORK</dt><dd>The staff loan file</dd></div>
				<div><dt>PLATFORM</dt><dd>Internal workspace</dd></div>
			</dl>
		</section>
		<div class="site-container">
			<figure class="file-flow" aria-label="Illustration of the staff workspace. Sample data.">
				<div class="file-flow-bar"><span>VASTER <i>/</i> STAFF WORKSPACE</span><span>ILLUSTRATION · SAMPLE DATA</span></div>
				<div class="file-flow-body">
					<article>
						<p>01</p>
						<h2>The deal arrives.</h2>
						<p>Example Holdings asks for a sample bridge loan. The deal lands in the CRM, and the workspace opens one file for it.</p>
					</article>
					<article>
						<p>02</p>
						<h2>The papers get checked.</h2>
						<p>Insurance, the appraisal, and the entity documents sit on that file. A person accepts or rejects what the papers say.</p>
					</article>
					<article>
						<p>03</p>
						<h2>The committee gets a link.</h2>
						<p>The packet is a link, not a document rebuilt that morning. The tables are calculated. A person edits the brief and decides.</p>
					</article>
				</div>
				<figcaption>Illustration of the staff workspace. Sample deal. Not a production result.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
		<section class="case-narrative site-container section-pad">
			<div>
				<h2>The same loan used to be assembled by hand.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="case-prose">
				<p class="case-prose-lead">Committee packets were a document someone built from the CRM, a folder, and a spreadsheet. It was hard to see which number came from a record and which number was still a guess.</p>
				<p>The staff workspace keeps one loan file. The committee opens a link. A person approves the facts, edits the brief, and decides whether to lend. Borrowers do not use this workspace.</p>
			</div>
		</section>
		<section class="result-callout site-container">
			<p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal-dot"></span> THE RESULT</p>
			<p>Committee packets went from a hand-built document to a link.</p>
		</section>
		<div class="site-container case-related">
			<a class="related-project" href="/work/vaster">
				<div>
					<span class="section-kicker">THE BORROWER PORTAL</span>
					<h3>Vaster borrower portal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></h3>
					<p>Borrower intake, CRM records, and signing. A different product from this workspace.</p>
				</div>
				<span class="related-project-path" aria-hidden="true">INTAKE → SIGNATURE</span>
			</a>
		</div>
		<section class="closing-section dark-surface">
			<div class="site-container closing-inner">
				<p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal-dot"></span> THE NEXT STEP</p>
				<h2>Send one loan file.</h2>
				<div class="closing-bottom">
					<p>We’ll show you where it gets retyped and mock up the fix on sample data, free.</p>
					<a class="action action-lime" href="/contact">Send me a file walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
<style>
	.case-title-row h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
	.case-title-row { flex-wrap: wrap; }
	.case-deck { max-width: 22ch; }
	.file-flow {
		border: 1px solid #c9d4c2;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: #f7f8f4;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.file-flow-bar, .file-flow figcaption {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: .8rem 1.1rem;
		background: #1a2018;
		color: #d5e0cc;
		font: .68rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);
		letter-spacing: .06em;
	}
	.file-flow-bar i { font-style: normal; color: #8ea384; padding-inline: .35rem; }
	.file-flow-body {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
	}
	.file-flow-body article {
		padding: 1.6rem 1.4rem 1.8rem;
		border-top: 0;
	}
	.file-flow-body article + article { border-left: 1px solid #d5dece; }
	.file-flow-body article > p:first-child {
		margin: 0;
		font: .7rem/1.4 var(--font-mono);
		letter-spacing: .08em;
		color: #5d6e52;
	}
	.file-flow-body h2 {
		margin: .8rem 0 .7rem;
		font: 500 1.45rem/1.25 var(--font-display);
		letter-spacing: -.04em;
	}
	.file-flow-body article p:last-child {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--color-muted);
		line-height: 1.7;
	}
	.file-flow figcaption { justify-content: flex-start; }
	.result-callout { padding-block: 1rem 3.5rem; }
	.result-callout .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
	.result-callout > p:last-child {
		max-width: 16ch;
		margin: 0;
		font: 500 clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.6rem)/1.15 var(--font-display);
		letter-spacing: -.05em;
	}
	@media (max-width: 850px) {
		.file-flow-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.file-flow-body article + article { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid #d5dece; }
		.case-deck { max-width: 28ch; }
	}
</style>
